{
  "slug": "scriptorium-cowork",
  "name": "Scriptorium Cowork",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Scriptorium guides students and researchers from a half-formed topic to a defensible literature review. Directive interview, research-question elicitation, PRISMA-audited search and synthesis, and optional NotebookLM publishing.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **14 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (14): `audit` (Use when the user asks for the audit trail, PRISMA flow, or a record of what happened during…), `contradictions` (Use when the user asks where papers disagree, wants to surface contradictions, or is preparing a \"limits of…), `extract` (Use when the user asks to pull full text of kept papers, extract methods/findings, or populate evidence from…), `grill-question` (Use when the user has a topic and a clear intent to write a research-paper-shaped artifact (paper, chapter,…), `publish` (Use when the user asks for a podcast, slide deck, mind map, or video of a finished review), `render` (Use when the user has a finished synthesis (synthesis.md + corpus.jsonl + evidence.jsonl) and wants a click-to-source viewer…), `research-direction` (Use when the user has a research topic but doesn't yet know what they want from engaging with…), `review` (Use when the user asks to run a lit review on a topic or research question end-to-end (\"run…), and 6 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install scriptorium-cowork@claude-community` from `Jerrymwolf/Scriptorium-Cowork`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
  "sourceType": "community",
